    "result_text": "All tests pass (`AcceptanceTest` is the sole test class; the other two files are its base/support). The full build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented optional, city-region-validated `postcode` support for owners.\n\n**Contract (OpenAPI)** \u2014 `src/main/resources/openapi.yml`: added a `postcode` property to the `OwnerFields` schema (`type: string`, `pattern: ^[0-9]{4}$`), left out of `required`. This regenerates `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` with `getPostcode()`/`setPostcode()`, and the 4-digit format check is enforced by the existing `ValidateOwnerFields` step (so `\"12\"` \u2192 400).\n\n**Domain + persistence** \u2014 added a `postcode` column/field with accessors to `Owner.java`, and a `postcode` column to all four schema dialects (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`). MapStruct auto-maps the field in both directions, so it's stored on create and returned on read.\n\n**Region-range policy** \u2014 new `util/PostcodeRange.java`: a small, single-responsibility util holding the fixed region\u2192range table (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099). It reuses the existing `CityRegion` lookup to resolve a city's region, and returns `true` (accept any 4-digit) when the region is unknown.\n\n**Validation step** \u2014 new `ValidateOwnerPostcode` function: skips when postcode is absent (optional), otherwise rejects with `InvalidOwnerFieldsException` (400, naming `postcode`) when out of range. Wired as a `validatePostcode` step after `validate` in both `owners.POST.yml` and `owners/{ownerId}.PUT.yml`, and `ApplyOwner` now copies postcode on update.\n\nEach concern landed in its own unit: format in the DTO, the region table in `CityRegion`, the range table in `PostcodeRange`, and the cross-field check in a dedicated pipeline step \u2014 nothing was bolted onto an existing catch-all.",
